<bx:include template="../partials/_head.bxm">
<bx:output>
<div class="container">
	<div class="narrow">
		<header class="page-head about-head">
			<bx:if len( data.author.getAvatarUrl() )>
				<img src="#encodeForHTMLAttribute( data.author.getAvatarUrl() )#" alt="" class="about-head__avatar" width="72" height="72">
			</bx:if>
			<div>
				<h1 class="page-head__title">#encodeForHTML( data.author.getDisplayName() )#</h1>
				<p class="page-head__lede">Senior software developer specializing in ColdFusion and BoxLang.</p>
			</div>
		</header>

		<div class="about-body">
			<p>I'm a senior software developer with many years of experience in CFML, from long-running tag-based applications to modern BoxLang. Most of my professional work is in e-commerce integration: connecting platforms such as Shopify, Amazon, eBay and Walmart so that inventory, orders and fulfillment stay accurate across every sales channel.</p>
			<p>I also build open-source tools for the BoxLang ecosystem. <a href="/projects/boxlang-express">boxlang-express</a>, an Express.js-style web framework, started because nothing like it existed; this site runs on it. Other work includes modules for ActivityPub federation, GraphQL and passkey authentication. They're all on the <a href="/projects">projects page</a>.</p>
			<p>I care about systems with clear rules, code that's easy to maintain and documentation that explains why things are the way they are. Outside of work I read a lot of science fiction and fantasy, and train calisthenics.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<bx:if data.latestPosts.len()>
<div class="container">
	<div class="narrow">
		<section class="home-block">
			<div class="block-head">
				<h2 class="block-head__title">Recent writing</h2>
				<a href="/posts" class="block-head__more">All writing &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="entry-list">
				<bx:loop array="#data.latestPosts#" item="post">
					<bx:include template="../partials/postEntry.bxm">
				</bx:loop>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</div>
</bx:if>
</bx:output>
<bx:include template="../partials/_foot.bxm">
